Editable JSON source format
---------------------------
Each phase file only keeps fields that humans should edit:

    {
      "stage": {
        "id": 3,
        "label": "03 Foreman-A Build Sub Blueprint",
        "summary": "Foreman-A spends this phase building Region-A.",
        "metrics": ["00:55.0", "04:10.0", "Region-A build"],
        "children": [
          { "id": "3.1", "label": "split sub blueprint", "summary": "Foreman-A splits Region-A into worker subtasks." }
        ]
      },
      "events": [
        {
          "time": "00:55.0",
          "actor": "Foreman-A",
          "kind": "TOOL",
          "action": "Inspect sub blueprint before building Region-A.",
          "sublines": [
            "tool_call: Read Sub Blueprint[Region-A.json] -> success, 42 subtasks, Workers 001-020"
          ],
          "tool": "Read Sub Blueprint"
        }
      ]
    }

Do not hand-edit rendered cache fields such as text, line, lines, seq, display, or timecode.
The frontend generates those fields at runtime.

Event kind rule
---------------
Keep the visible demo labels very simple:

    LOG      ordinary event, status, coordination, verification, cleanup, or progress
    TOOL     an agent calls a tool
    SKILL    an agent learns, publishes, or uses a skill

System events should stay LOG. Tools are only for agents.
Avoid extra labels such as BOOT, PLAN, INPUT, AGENTS, COORD, CHECK, PASS, CLEAN, TOOL✓, SKILL◆, or SKILL↗ in the visible demo log.

Subline rule
------------
The main event sentence should stay readable on its own.
Sublines belong to the immediately previous main event.
A tool call and its result should stay together in the same subline.

Good:
    Worker-021: I can use Build Region for Region-B/subtask-017.
        -> skill_call: Use Skill[Build Region, Region-B/subtask-017] -> success, script generated from shared placement pattern

Avoid:
    Separate event for tool call.
    Separate event for tool result.

Skill placement rule
--------------------
Skills are not standalone stages.
They appear inside the Foreman build files because they are learned while work is happening.

Recommended skill story:

    Foreman-A Build Sub Blueprint
        early tool-heavy building
        Build Region is learned after repeated read/generate/run/verify/submit loops

    Foreman-B Build Sub Blueprint
        Build Region is reused
        Replace Region is learned after repeated repair/mismatch patches

    Foreman-C Build Sub Blueprint
        Build Region and Replace Region are reused
        Scaffold is learned when tall or awkward regions need temporary support

    Foreman-D Build Sub Blueprint
        mostly skill-assisted building
        Build Region, Replace Region, and Scaffold are reused heavily

    Foreman-E Build Sub Blueprint
        late build and cleanup pressure
        Clean Region is learned when cleanup becomes a repeated task

    Close And Clean Environment
        Clean Region is reused for final cleanup

